Condition : 26 - Prior to occupation of any above ground works, full details of the proposed green roofs shall have been submitted to the Local Planning Authority for approval in writing, including planting schedules and maintenance and management arrangements. Details shall include:
i. Construction drawings to include a plan and cross sections;
ii. Native wildflower seed mix (turf or sedum blanket will not be accepted);
iii. Substrate between depth; undulating and containing different materials/sizes (sand, gravel, crushed ceramic, brick, recycled, inert materials);
iv. Small piles of untreated logs; No irrigation;
v. Confirmation that the green roof construction will be supervised by a suitable, qualified landscape/ecology contractor;
vi. Details of solar panels, location and specification; The approved details shall be implemented and retained permanently thereafter.
Reason: In order to ensure a satisfactory appearance of the site and the area and to promote biodiversity.

Condition : 36 - No development shall take place until an Ecological Management Plan and Construction Environmental Management Plan has been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority.
The Plans shall incorporate:
(i) details of measures to protect breeding birds, nests and eggs from mortality/damage, injury and disturbance, including avoidance by timing and/or appropriate supervision;
(ii) details of the ecological clerk of works supervision to be put in place to monitor the clearance of vegetation to ensure no impact on undiscovered or other unexpected faunal encounters;
(iii) an ecological lighting plan;
(iv) details of ecological enhancement and urban greening factor, including how the urban greening factor is to be delivered and achieved on site;
(v) details of how the enhancement measures will be monitored, managed and maintained, including the long- term design objectives, management responsibilities and maintenance schedules;
(vi) additional detail on location and type of bird/bat boxes, maintenance and a commitment that any data collected is to be shared with the Council;
(vii) species surveys within and around the site to demonstrate ecological enhancements
The development shall then be carried out in accordance with the approved details during the construction period and after development.
Reason: In the interests of nature conservation.
